% CODA, bars 325-376 (c030: header renumbered from the v03 numbers 333-384; the finale thread reads these bar numbers).
% c022: iv6 at 331 (C-E-A over C, Phrygian approach to V; c022 called it 339 in v23 numbers) replaces the diminished triad C sharp-E-G (A-S PDF 167 Ex. 11-6c, 168): Vln I C-A, Cl 2, Bsn 2, Cb, Cbsn on C, Bsn 1 A; no G, so no C-major triad.
% 325-340 Più mosso: motive x as a stretto ostinato entering from the bottom (Vc 325, Vla 326, Vln II 327, Vln I 328), pp crescendo; the bass falls
%   E-D-C-B (329-332); theme A's head ff (333); Vln I and Fl 1 peak on B6 at 336, fff, the movement's only fff (the scherzo's highest note, a semitone under the finale's C7);
%   hemiola 337-338, E minor chord (339), general pause (340).
% 341-376 Meno mosso (tempo del Trio), T returns p in Hn 1 (341), Cl 1 (345), Vln I and Fl 1 (349), cadence 355.
%   c013: T's first half (341-348) is in A major, the tonicized IV that a late coda can carry (Aldwell-Schachter Unit 26 sec. 11, PDF 451-452);
%   its half cadence on E (348, V of A) is the pivot back to E (I), and T's second half (349-356) confirms E with ii-ii6-6/4-V-I.
% 357-360: Hn 1 sings the motto's chromatic tail on the fifth degree, B-A sharp-A-G sharp (E flat-D-D flat-C transposed),
%   over E - A sharp dim7 - A minor (iv, mixture) - E: a plagal close that ends on G sharp.
% 361-376: E major held pp, then only Hn 1 and Vln I on G sharp (the pitch that opened the scherzo, movement II's A flat) over a timpani roll (372-374)
%   and a last pizzicato E with the harp's harmonics (375); the finale takes that G sharp as A flat (Hn 1 A flat 4, Vln I A flat 5).

% c028: 325-328 the ostinato entries stay pp until Vln I has entered (328); all strings cresc. from 328, mf at 329, ff at 333 (Adler II PDF 37: hold back for the event).
% c028: 336 fff in all parts: Vln I's B6 and the timpani roll are the movement's peak, above the ff of 72, 104-120, 300-320 and 333 (Adler II PDF 38-40, Tchaikovsky 4/i).
% c032: 329-332 Vln I in 10ths above the falling bass (G-F#-E-D#, with Cl 1 an octave lower), not in octaves with it; the E-B drone gives way
%   to chord tones at 331 (iv6: A-E) and 332 (V: B-F#) in Vc, Vla, Vln II, so no B sounds against the bass C before the bass reaches B (A-S Unit 17, PDF 267-269, 277-279).
codaFluteOne = { R2.*8 | e'''4-.\ff b''8-. b''-. e'''4-. | g'''2->( fis'''8 f'''8 | e'''4-.) b''8-. b''-. g'''4-. | b'''2.->\fff | a'''2-> fis'''4~ | fis'''4 dis'''2 | e'''4-> r4 r4 | R2. | R2.*8 | cis'''2(\pp dis'''4 | e'''4 gis'''2) | a'''4.( gis'''8 fis'''4) | cis'''4( b'' a'') | gis''4( b'' e''') | dis'''2( fis'''4) | e'''2.~ | e'''2 r4 | R2.*4 | gis''2.\pp | gis''2.~ | gis''2.~ | gis''2 r4 | R2.*12 | }
% c029: 333-339 Fl 2 and Ob 2 fill the chord above the trumpets (Rimsky-Korsakov PDF 110-111): at 336 B6-D#6-B5-F#5-D#5 over Tpt B4-D#4 (was B-B-B-B).
